Belfry
A bare stone room under the bell.  A rope hangs from it, beside a rusty lever,
and there is a niche in the wall.

You can see a hammer and a feather here.

>look
Belfry
A bare stone room under the bell.  A rope hangs from it, beside a rusty lever,
and there is a niche in the wall.

You can see a hammer and a feather here.

>toll bell
BONG.  The note rolls out over the town.

>x bell
A great bronze bell, still humming.

>toll rope
BONG.  The note rolls out over the town.

>pull rope
BONG.  The note rolls out over the town.

>toll rag
The oily rag is not something you can toll.

>toll
What do you want to toll?

>sing
Your voice echoes round the stone walls.

The bell’s hum dies away.

>peal bell
BONG.  The note rolls out over the town.

>ring bell
BONG.  The note rolls out over the town.

>ring rope
BONG.  The note rolls out over the town.

>ring rag
The oily rag isn’t something you can ring.

>leap
You jump on the spot, fruitlessly.

The bell’s hum dies away.

>pull lever
The lever is rusted solid.

>clean lever
(with the oily rag)
The rust comes away on the rag.

>clean lever with rag
The lever is already quite clean enough.

>x lever
An iron lever, bright and clean.

>pull lever
A trapdoor opens in the floor, and the game is done.

>take feather
Taken.

>put feather in niche
The niche is for the rag.

>put rag in niche
You put the oily rag in the niche.

>turn dial to 2
Okay, you turn the chime dial to 2.

>set dial to 5
The dial goes from 1 to 3.

>x dial
A brass dial for the chimes, set to 2.

>shout hello
“HELLO!” you shout, and the bell hums.

>hit bell
(first taking the hammer)
CLANG.  Not the note the bell was cast for.

